        "title": "The Scientific Revolution - What Actually Changed and Why",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The Scientific Revolution (roughly 1543-1687) spans Copernicus's *De Revolutionibus* to Newton's *Principia*. The conventional story — \"science replaced superstition\" — is too simple. What actually changed was: the relationship between mathematics and physical description, the role of experiment as arbiter, and the organizational infrastructure of knowledge production."
